 - `strategy: ratchet` is optional and only for a `preventive` control, with `baseline-source` (the path of its JSON baseline file, a list of unique names), `owner` and `exit`, all three. It says the control is a temporary ratchet, not a station mode. The three fields without it are listed as a problem. See `references/modes.md`.
 - `evidence` is optional and says what the control needs before it may claim `tested`. Evidence is the control's own Test Cases run against an X, so it adds no new kind of test: `evidence: [fixture:3, merge:2, provoked:1:fail]` is a list of `<x>:<runs>`, each x once, runs from 1, and it reads: at least that many runs of the Cases of this control against that kind of X. An X is any lower-case word the control chooses for what a Case ran against: a fixture, a real merge or a change under review, a provoked case, a before and after pair of trees. At least one entry ends `:fail`: an X that is a real failure, so a Case that is GREEN on it, where the same Case was RED on that failure without the control's mechanism, shows the control rightly caught it. See `references/judging-status.md`.
 - It stores no state and no pointer to its test. A Case that tests the control points back to it with a first line `// Case <id> tests: <control id>`, and sits beside the control, as `CTL<n>-<slug>/CTL<n>.md` and `T<n>.test.mjs`.
-- Ids are unique. A change identifier is not a control id.
